                        <msContents><summary>Royal Chronicles from Dabra Libānos and Dabra Karbe</summary>
                            <msItem xml:id="p1_i1">
                                <locus from="1" to="73"/>
                                <title>Royal chronicle from Dabra Libānos</title>
                                <note>Royal chronicle in Amharic, according to a note on <locus target="#IIIr"/> (<ref target="#a1"/>) copied
                                    from a manuscript, which is possibly from the property of <persName ref="PRS8802seyyumM"/>.
                                    The text occupies the left-hand pages, which bear odd page numbers. At various places, some passages with unclear
                                    readings have been left blank and some of them filled with pencil, e.g. <locus target="#13 #15"/>.</note>
                                <msItem xml:id="p1_i1.1">
                                    <locus from="1"/>
                                    <title>Journey of the Queen of Sheba and the coronation of the Kings of ʾAksum</title>
                                    <note>Beginning of the Royal Chronicle with the journey of the 
                                        <persName ref="PRS6541Makedda">Queen of Sheba</persName> to <placeName ref="LOC3957Jerusa"/>,
                                        the coronation of the Kings of <placeName ref="LOC7363Aksum"/>, <persName ref="PRS7005Menilek"/>, etc.
                                    </note>
                                    <incipit xml:lang="am">ከኢየሩሳሌም፡ የወጡ፡ ፲፪ ሹማሞች፡ እነዚህ፡ ናቸው። በአኵስምም፡ ንጉሥ፡ በነገሠ፡ ጊዜ፡ ሠራዊቱ፡ እንደ፡ ሆሣዕና፡ የሰሌን፡ 
                                        ቅጸል፡ ይዘው፡ ካህናቱም፡ መስቀል፡ ጥና፡ ይዘው፡ ከዳዊት፡ በ፻፲፯ኛው፡ አንቀጽ፡ ቡሩክ፡ ዘይመጽእ፡ በስመ፡ እግዚአብሔር፡ እያሉ፡ ይዞራሉ። ኦሪት፡ 
                                        <sic>ነብያት፡</sic> ወንጌል፡ ሐዋርያት፡ የካህናት፡ የመንግሥት፡ ነገር፡ የሚአነሣውን፡ እያነበቡ፡ ዳዊት፡ ሰሎሞን፡ እየደገሙ፡ ይጸልያሉ።</incipit>
                                </msItem>
                                <msItem xml:id="p1_i1.2">
                                    <locus from="21"/>
                                    <title ref="LIT3854KingList" type="incomplete">Genealogy of the Ethiopian Kings</title>
                                    <note>A text that bears resemblances to that of the <ref type="work" corresp="LIT2352ShortC"/>, but does not
                                        follow it exactly. This list ends with the reign of <persName ref="PRS6229LebnaDe"/>.</note>
                                    <incipit xml:lang="am">ከዚህ፡ በኋላ፡ የኢትዮጵያን፡ ነገሥታት፡ የተውልዳቸውን፡ ታሪክ፡ እንጽፋለን። ሰሎሞን፡ ዕብነ፡ ሐኪምን፡ ወለደ፤ ይኸውም፡ 
                                        ምኒልክ፡ ነው። እናቱ፡ የአዜብ፡ ንግሥት፡ ናት፡ ስሟም፡ ማክዳ፡ ይባላል። ዕብነ፡ ሐኪም፡ ቶማይን፡ ወለደ። ቶማይ፡ ዘግዱርን፤</incipit>
                                    <explicit xml:lang="am">ከዚህ፡ በኋላ፡ ልጁ፡ ልብነ፡ ድንግል፡ ፴፫ ዓመት፡ ነገሠ። ስመ፡ መንግሥቱም፡ ወናግ፡ ሰገድ፡ ይባል፡ ነበር። እሱንም፡ ከእስላም፡
                                        የተወለድ፡ ግራኝ፡ የሚባል፡ ሰው፡ ተነስቶ፡ ከሸዋ፡ እስከ፡ ምጽዋ፡ አሳደደው። አብያተ፡ ክርስቲያናትን፡ ሁሉ፡ ተኰሰ፡ በሸዋ፤ በአምሐራ፤ በበጌምድር፤ በደንቢያ፡ 
                                        እስከ፡ ተከዜ፡ ድረስ፡ ያሉትን፡ የክርስቲያን፡ ልጆች፡ ፈጃቸው። ። ።</explicit>
                                </msItem>
                                <msItem xml:id="p1_i1.3">
                                    <locus from="53" to="71"/>
                                    <title>History of Grañ</title>
                                    <note>Dedicated to the war against Grañ. The chronicle stops with <persName ref="PRS4428Galawdew"/>
                                        (1540–1559) and the death of the king’s sister, Wayzaro Walatta Qǝddusān.</note>
                                    <incipit xml:lang="am">እጽሕፍ፡ ነገረ፡ ግራኝ፤ የተነሳበት፡ ምክንያቱ፡ እንዲህ፡ ነው። በሱ፡ እጅ፡ ያላቁት፡ የሞቱት፡ የተሰደዱት፡ ፺፪፼ከ፫ሽህ፡ 
                                        ከ፰፻ከ፺፭ናቸው። ዜናቸውን፡ እንጽፋለን፡ የሰማው፡ ሰው፡ ሁሉ፡ በሃይማኖት፡ እንዲጸና። የግራኝ፡ የልደቱ፡ ምክንያት፡ እንዲህ፡ ነው። አሕመድ፡ የሚባል፡ እስላም፡
                                        ሐረርጌንና፡ አዳልን፡ የሚገዛ፡ ነበር።</incipit>
                                    <explicit xml:lang="am">አጽናፍ፡ ሰገድ፡ በነገሠ፡ በዓመት፡ ከ፭ወር፡ ከ፳፪ ቀን፡ ግራኝ፡ ሞተ። በሞተ፡ በ፪ ዓመቱ፡ አበሻን፡ ገደለው፡ አፍርንጅ፡ በብዙ፡ ሀገር፡
                                        ተማምለው፡ የኢትዮጵያን፡ ሲሶ፡ ሊሰጣቸው፡ ምሎ፡ ነበርና፡ ስለዚህ፡ ነገር፡ መኳንንቱ፡ ሊቃውንቱም፡ ከንጉሥ፡ ጋራ፡ ተጣሉ። ለምን፡ ሃይማኖት፡ ያጠፋሉ፡ ብለው፤
                                        ከዚህ፡ በኋላ፡ መከረው፡ ብዙ፡ ከበት፡ ሰጥተው፡ ከሀገራቸው፡ ሰደዷቸው። እሱም፡ የአፍርንጅን፡ ሃይማኖት፡ ወዶ፡ ነበር፡ አፍርንጅ፡ ሀገራቸው፡ ከሄደ፡ በኋላ፡ 
                                        በእስክንድርያ፡ ሃይማኖት፡ ፀና። አበሻ፡ በሞተ፡ በ፯ ዓመት፡ በ፯ ወር፡ አጽናፈ፤ ሰገድ፡ አዳል፡ ምድር፡ ዘመተ። በ፪ ዓመ<pb n="73"/>ት፡ ፀሐይ፡ ፀለመ። 
                                        በ፫ ዓመት፡ አዛዥ፡ ገርማሞ፡ አቤቶ፡ ያዕቆብ፡ ወይዘሮ፡ ወለተ፡ ቅዱሳን፡ ሞቱ። አጽናፍ፡ ሰገድ፡ በነገሠ፡ በ፱ ዓመት። የግራኝ።</explicit>
                                </msItem>
                                <colophon xml:id="coloph1">
                                    <locus target="#73"/>
                                    According to the colophon, this manuscript was copied from another manuscript that belonged to 
                                    <persName ref="PRS15511WaldaGi"><roleName type="title">Grāzmāč</roleName> Wareññā</persName> 
                                    and had been written by the scribe <persName ref="PRS15512Dagefe"/>—whose brother was 
                                    <persName ref="PRS15513FereSanbat"/>—at Dabra Libānos (to be identified with either 
                                    <placeName ref="LOC2296DabraL"/> or <placeName ref="LOC2297DabraL"/>).
                                    <q xml:lang="am">ዝንቱ፡ መጽሐፍ፡ ዘግራዝመች፤ ወሬኛ፡ ዘአጽሐፎ፡ በደብረ፡ ሊባኖስ፤ ወምስለ፡ ጸሐፊሁ፡ ኃጥእ፡ ወአባሲ፡ ደግፌ። ወንድሙ፡ ፍሬ፡ 
                                        ሰንበት፡ ለዓለመ፡ ዓለም፡ አሜን። ። ።</q>
                                </colophon>
                                <textLang xml:lang="am"/>
                            </msItem>
                            <msItem xml:id="p1_i2">
                                <locus from="77" to="109"/>
                                <title>Various documents from a Gospel from Dabra Karbe</title>
                                <note>According to a note on <locus target="#75"/> (<ref target="#a2"/>) copied from an old Gospel from the 
                                    church Dabra Karbe of Zānā.<!--  Issue #3371--> The documents are mentioned 
                                    and analysed in <bibl><ptr target="bm:Derat2006Royal"/></bibl>. At various places, some passages with unclear
                                    readings have been left blank and some of them filled with pencil, e.g. <locus target="#103 #105"/>. The entire texts
                                    of these documents and their translations as well as preceding notes by <persName ref="PRS3182ContiRo"/> are
                                    presented in <bibl><ptr target="bm:Derat2006Royal"/><citedRange unit="page">72–77</citedRange></bibl>.
                                        </note>
                                <textLang xml:lang="gez"/>
                                <msItem xml:id="p1_i2.1">
                                    <locus from="77" to="78"/>
                                    <title>Letter of the ʿaqqabe saʿat ʾAmmǝḫā Laṣǝyon to the monks of Dabra Karbe</title>
                                    <note>The text is preceded by a note on <locus target="76"/> (cf. <ref target="#a3"/> describing the position of the 
                                        text in the Vorlage manuscript directly after the Gospel of Matthew. The incipit was quoted from the Stefan Strelcyn’s
                                        catalogue, while the second quotation and the explicit and its translations are taken from 
                                        <bibl><ptr target="bm:Derat2006Royal"/><citedRange unit="page">67</citedRange></bibl>.</note>
                                    <incipit xml:lang="gez">እኤምሐክሙ፡ አነ፡
                                        <persName ref="PRS1881Ammehas"><roleName type="title">ዐቃቤ፡ ሰዓት፡</roleName> አምኃ፡ ለጽዮን።</persName> 
                                        ሰላም፡ ለክሙ፡ ኵልክሙ፡ ማኅበረ፡ ቅዱሳን፡ መነኮሳት፡ እለ፡ ሀሎክሙ፡ ውስተ፡ ደብረ፡ ከርቤ፡<!--  Issue #3371-->
                                    </incipit>
                                    <quote xml:lang="gez">ሰማዕኩ፡ አነ፡ ከመቦ፡ እምኔክሙ፡ እለ፡ ኢተሐውሩ፡ በኅገ፡ መነኮሳት፡ እንዘ፡ ትሰመዩ፡ ደቂቀ፡ ዚአየ፡ ወትንብሩ፡ ምስለ፡ ዓለም፡ 
                                        ገቢረክሙ፡ አብያት፡ ኀበ፡ ህልዋ፡ አንስት፡ ወካዕበ፡ ትትመየጡ፡ ውስተ፡ ደብረ፡ መነኮሳት።</quote>
                                    <quote xml:lang="en" type="translation">I have heard that some of you do not follow the rule of the monks. 
                                        Instead you are calling yourselves my children, you are living in the (secular) world, building houses near the 
                                        residence of the women. Then you come back in the monastery.</quote>
                                    <explicit xml:lang="gez">ወይጽሐፍዎ፡ ለዝንቱ፡ ክታበ፡ ውስተ፡ ወንጌል፡ ከመ፡ ይኩን፡ ሰምዐ፡ በቅድመ፡ እግዚአብሔር፡ ማእከሌየ፡ ወማእከሌክሙ።
                                            </explicit>
                                    <explicit xml:lang="en" type="translation">May this message be written in the Gospel, so that it will be a testimony
                                        before God, between me and you.</explicit>
                                </msItem>
                                <msItem xml:id="p1_i2.2">
                                    <locus from="81" to="93"/>
                                    <title type="incomplete" ref="LIT1955Mashaf">Fragments from the Maṣḥafa Milād</title>
                                    <note>The text occupies the left-hand pages, which bear odd page numbers. The text is preceded by a note in Italian 
                                        on <locus target="#79"/> (cf. <ref target="#a4"/>) describing the text and its position in the original manuscript.
                                        The beginning and the end are missing. It was described by <persName ref="PRS3182ContiRo"/> and
                                        <persName ref="PRS8999Strelcyn"/> as ‘History of Zarʾa Yāʿqob’, but identified as a fragment from the 
                                        <ref type="work" corresp="LIT1955Mashaf"/> by Marie-Laure Derat in <bibl><ptr target="bm:Derat2006Royal"/>
                                        <citedRange unit="page">65</citedRange></bibl>, i.e. "the lecture for taḥśaś 29, which is a celebration of king 
                                        Zärʾa Yaʿqob’s victory over Badlay at the battle of Gomit". According to Derat, the sequence of pages is arranged
                                        backward and the text is therefore in disorder.</note>
                                    <incipit xml:lang="gez"><supplied reason="lost" resp="PRS8999Strelcyn">እ</supplied>ምድኅረ፡ ሞኦሙ፡ ለጸላእቱ፡ 
                                        አዘዞሙ፡ ይኆልቁ፡ ኵሎ፡ አፍራሰ፡ ድርዕ፡ ወውላድ፡ ወሌጣ፡ አፍራሰ፡ <sic>ወቱኆለቈ፡</sic> ልብሰ፡ ሐጺን፡ ጽሩር፡ ዘምስለ፡ ድርዕ፡ ወሐምበል፡ በበድላይ፡ 
                                        ወዘሰራዊቱ፡ ወኮነ፡ ኆልቆሙ፡ አርባዕተ፡ እልፍ፡ ወአፍራስ፡ እለ፡ ይለብሱ፡ ልብሰ፡ ክሸድ፡ ስድስተ፡ ምእት፡</incipit>
                                </msItem>
                                <msItem xml:id="p1_i2.3">
                                    <locus from="97" to="99"/>
                                    <title>Announcement by Nagada ʾIyasus</title>
                                    <note>An announcement made by 
                                        <persName ref="PRS7458NagadaI"><roleName type="title">ʿaqāba Saʿāt</roleName> Nagada ʾIyasus</persName>  
                                        stating that the monastery of Dabra Karbe<!-- Issue --> must follow the
                                        rules established by <persName ref="PRS10626ZaraY"/> and <persName ref="PRS1881Ammehas"/> for Dabra
                                        Nagʷadgʷād, which could either be identified with <placeName ref="LOC2329DabraN"/> or with
                                        <placeName ref="INS0327DHE"/>, but according to <bibl><ptr target="bm:Derat2006Royal"/>
                                            <citedRange unit="page">70</citedRange></bibl>, <placeName ref="LOC2329DabraN"/> is more probable.
                                        The announcement is followed by a list of the monastery’s possessions. 
                                        The document is thought to date from the time of <persName ref="PRS10626ZaraY"/> despite the difference in
                                        time. The text occupies the left-hand pages, which bear odd page numbers. The text is preceded by a note in Italian
                                        on <locus target="#96"/> (cf. <ref target="#a5"/>) describing the text and its position in the original manuscript.
                                        The following incipit is taken from the catalogue description by Stefan Strelcyn, while the translation is from 
                                        <bibl><ptr target="bm:Derat2006Royal"/><citedRange unit="page">70</citedRange></bibl>.</note>
                                    <incipit xml:lang="gez">ወልኡክ፡ ሰርፄ፡ ወልዱ፡ ዜኑ። ዐምዱ። ጸሐፍኩ፡ ወአውገዝኩ፡ አነ፡ ነገደ፡ ኢየሱስ፡ ዓቃቤ፡ ሰዓት፡ አእሚርየ፡ ዘከመ፡ ሠርዑ፡ 
                                        ንጉሥነ፡ ዘርአ፡ ያዕቆብ፡ ወዓቃቤ፡ ሰዓት፡ አምኃ፡ ለጽዮን፡ ለካህናተ፡ ደብረ፡ ከርቤ፡ ከመ፡ ደብረ፡ ነጐድጓድ፡</incipit>
                                    <incipit xml:lang="en" type="translation"><gap reason="omitted"/> I have written and I have threatened of 
                                        excommunication, I, Nägädä Iyäsus, ʿaqqabe säʿat, learning how our king Zärʾa Yaʿqob and ʿaqqabe säʿat ʾAmḫa 
                                        Laṣǝyon, made the rules for the priests of Däbrä Kärbe like (those) of Däbrä Nägʷädgʷad.</incipit>
                                </msItem>
                                <msItem xml:id="p1_i2.4">
                                    <locus from="101" to="107"/>
                                    <title>Śǝrʿatā dabtarā</title>
                                    <note>Regulation by <persName ref="PRS10626ZaraY"/> on the dabtarā. Two ʿaqābe saʿāt are mentioned on
                                        <locus target="#103"/>: <persName ref="PRS7458NagadaI"/> and <persName ref="PRS1881Ammehas"/>.
                                        The text occupies the left-hand pages, which bear odd page numbers. The text is preceded by a note in Italian on 
                                        <locus target="#100"/> (cf. <ref target="#a6"/>) describing the text and its position in the original manuscript.
                                    </note>
                                    <incipit xml:lang="gez">ሥርዓተ፡ ደብተራ፡ ዘሠርዓ፡ ንጉሥነ፡ ዘርአ፡ ያዕቆብ፡ ርቱዓ፡ ሀይማኖት፡ ወአቡነ፡ አምኃ፡ ለጽዮን፡ ዓቃቤ፡ ሰዓት። ሥርዓተ፡ 
                                        ደብተራ፡ ዘደብረ፡ ከርቤ፡ ኆልቆ፡ ለካህናት፡ ፵ወ፯፡ ለጸሎት፡ ወለሰዓታት፡ ዘሌሊት፡ ወዘመዐልት፡ በእንተ፡ መድኃኒተ፡ ነፍሶሙ።</incipit>
                                </msItem>
                                <msItem xml:id="p1_i2.5">
                                    <locus target="#109"/>
                                    <title>Donation by śǝyyum Mazmura Dǝngǝl</title>
                                    <note>Donation, which was granted by the śǝyyum of <placeName ref="LOC6434Zana">Zānā</placeName>, 
                                        <persName ref="PRS15515MazmuraDen">Mazmura Dǝngǝl</persName> from the land of ʿĀdd Mǝrwā, which
                                        is probably <placeName ref="LOC4597Marwa"/> to the monastery of Dabra Karbe of Zānā.<!--Issue #3371 -->
                                        The text occupies the left-hand pages, which bear odd page numbers. The text is preceded by a note in Italian on 
                                        <locus target="#108"/> (cf. <ref target="#a7"/>) describing the text and its position in the original manuscript.
                                        According to information given by Stefan Strelcyn in <bibl><ptr target="bm:Strelcyn1976Catalogue"/>
                                            <citedRange unit="item">91, II, 5</citedRange><citedRange unit="page">240</citedRange></bibl>, this
                                        text ranges up to fol. 114, but according to his information in a note on the following page, the fols. 110 to 115 are 
                                        occupied by another text on another type of paper.</note>
                                    <incipit xml:lang="gez">ይጽሐፍ፡ መዝሙረ፡ ድንግል፡ ሥዩመ፡ ዛና፡ ወሀብኩ፡ ዓድ፡ ምረዋ፡ ዘነበረ፡ ጥንተ፡ በእደዊሃ፡ ለደብረ፡ ከርቤ፡ ከመ፡ ይኵኖሙ፡
                                        መርሐ፡ ለመንግሥተ፡ ሰማያት፡</incipit>
                                </msItem>
                            </msItem>
